# svrnty self-host — environment template.
# For Docker self-host (recommended): copy to `.env` (gitignored), fill in, then run
#   `docker compose up -d --build`.  For a direct `next start` run instead: copy to `.env.local`.
# NEVER commit real secrets. Full guide: docs/SELF_HOSTING.md.

# ── Domain: the one knob that makes a self-hosted instance YOURS ──────────────
# Your bare domain (no scheme). Every share link (/c/<code>), claimed-slug URL, and
# display string points here. Default is the managed nursery svrnty.is — a DEFAULT,
# not a dependency ("the tree in the seed"): a self-certifying durable_id needs no
# permission from svrnty.is to relocate. See src/lib/config/domain.ts.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SVRNTY_DOMAIN=svrnty.is

# Optional: override the scheme+host explicitly. Defaults to https://$NEXT_PUBLIC_SVRNTY_DOMAIN.
# Set this for http / localhost during development.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SVRNTY_BASE_URL=https://svrnty.is

# ── Email (identity verification, via Resend) ────────────────────────────────
# The "from" address for verification emails — a sender your provider has verified
# for YOUR domain. Defaults to verify@svrnty.is (only valid on the managed instance).
EMAIL_FROM=verify@svrnty.is

# Resend API key (https://resend.com/api-keys). SERVER-SIDE ONLY — must never be a
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ var (that would ship the secret to the browser bundle).
RESEND_API_KEY=

# ── Full nursery (optional — vanity slugs on your own domain) ─────────────────
# Leave unset for a minimal self-host: identity is self-certifying, so the slug routes
# simply return "unavailable" and everything else works. To offer vanity slugs
# (id.example.com/alice), run the registration backend:
#   docker compose --profile nursery up -d --build
# Keep the service host as "registration" — one slug route hardcodes it (compose sets
# SATELLITE_URL for you, so you rarely need to override it).
# SATELLITE_URL=http://registration:8101
#
# Image for the registration backend (built from infra/svrnty — see SELF_HOSTING.md).
# REGISTRATION_IMAGE=svrnty-registration:latest
